  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gridworks Guarantee premium Amari Power Transmission project Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gridworks&apos; subsidiary GW Uganda Investments LLP (UK) applied for and has been awarded NOK 25 million in support for guarantee premiums to be charged by guarantors or insurers in the first independent power transmission project in Uganda. The Amari Transmission Project is a pilot for private investments in transmission infrastructure in Africa and is developed in close cooperation with the state utility Uganda Electricity Transmission Company Limited UETCL. The investor will buy political risk insurance for their investment in new transformers to be installed at UETCL&apos;s substations to improve the transmission network in Uganda to enable evacuation of power generated.</narrative>
  </description>
